CM_ "Generated from the uploaded 43009 CAN specification excerpt. Default module source address is fixed to 0xD9 in this file. Proprietary A control/response messages use fixed controller source address 0xD1 to match production firmware behavior. Several source tables show decimal 224 alongside hex 0xD9; this DBC follows 0xD9 / 217 because the summary tables and hex fields are internally consistent. AD4 is encoded on 0x18FF18D9 because section 8.10 shows PF/PS 0xFF/0x18 even though the section heading says PGN 65305.";
CM_ BO_ 2565855697 "J1939 Proprietary A control request. Controller source address is fixed at 0xD1 in this DBC, so runtime CAN ID is 0x18EFD9D1. Byte1 is modeled as a 6-bit command code plus a 2-bit prefix. The provided excerpt is inconsistent about the special raw bytes 0xFE and 0xFF, so those cases are documented through the prefix plus command-code combination rather than a separate full-byte signal.";
CM_ SG_ 2565855697 Command "Logical command code from Byte1 bits 0..5. Known values in the excerpt are 0x00, 0x01, 0x10, 0x11, and 0x20. The summary table also lists special raw bytes 0xFE and 0xFF; these cannot be represented by the 6-bit code alone, so inspect Reserved_Prefix as well.";
CM_ SG_ 2565855697 Reserved_Prefix "Byte1 bits 6..7. Normal command diagrams show a fixed prefix value of binary 10, which decodes here as raw value 2. Special summary-table bytes 0xFE and 0xFF would decode with prefix 3.";
CM_ SG_ 2565855697 Bit_Rate_Set "The excerpt says this byte is CAN bit rate divided by 1000 and that valid values are 250k or 500k. Because the field is only 8 bits wide, 500 cannot be represented literally, so this signal is left as the raw code from the table.";
CM_ BO_ 2565853657 "J1939 Proprietary A response. Controller source address is fixed at 0xD1 in this DBC, so runtime CAN ID is 0x18EFD1D9. Response 0x20 payload interpretation depends on the previously requested Information Index, so Byte2..Byte7 are exposed as generic data bytes.";
CM_ SG_ 2565853657 Response "Logical response code from Byte1 bits 0..5. Response payload mirrors the corresponding command layout according to the excerpt.";
CM_ SG_ 2565853657 Reserved_Prefix "Byte1 bits 6..7. Normal response diagrams show a fixed prefix value of binary 10, which decodes here as raw value 2.";
CM_ SG_ 2565853657 Active_Protocol_Mode "Active Protocol Mode";
CM_ SG_ 2565853657 Active_Fault_Code "Active fault code. Value table is populated from section 9 fault codes.";
CM_ SG_ 2565853657 UserID "User ID [ID1]";
CM_ SG_ 2565853657 Software_Version "Firmware Version";
CM_ SG_ 2565853657 Software_Revision "Firmware Revision";
CM_ SG_ 2565853657 Info_Data_Byte2 "For response 0x20, Byte2..Byte7 contain either packed part-number nibbles or MAC address bytes depending on the Information Index that was requested.";
CM_ BO_ 2566854105 "Digital input status. All status items are 2-bit fields. The provided excerpt names the fields but does not define the semantic mapping of raw values 0..3, so they are left as raw 2-bit values.";
CM_ SG_ 2566854105 Input_1A "I/O Status 1A";
CM_ SG_ 2566854105 Input_1B "I/O Status 1B";
CM_ SG_ 2566854105 Input_2A "I/O Status 2A";
CM_ SG_ 2566854105 Input_2B "I/O Status 2B";
CM_ SG_ 2566854105 Input_3A "I/O Status 3A";
CM_ SG_ 2566854105 Input_3B "I/O Status 3B";
CM_ SG_ 2566854105 Input_4A "I/O Status 4A";
CM_ SG_ 2566854105 Input_4B "I/O Status 4B";
CM_ SG_ 2566854105 MagSensor "Mag Sensor";
CM_ SG_ 2566854105 SpwrStat1 "Sensor Power 1 Status";
CM_ SG_ 2566854105 SpwrStat2 "Sensor Power 2 Status";
CM_ SG_ 2566854105 SpwrStat3 "Sensor Power 3 Status";
CM_ SG_ 2566854105 SpwrStat4 "Sensor Power 4 Status";
CM_ BO_ 2566854361 "Analog ports 1A, 1B, 2A, and 2B. Documented range is 0..5000 counts for 0..5 V. This DBC scales to volts using 0.001 V per bit. When ratiometric mode is enabled, the values represent ratio voltage per the specification.";
CM_ SG_ 2566854361 Port_1A "Analog Port1A";
CM_ SG_ 2566854361 Port_1B "Analog Port1B";
CM_ SG_ 2566854361 Port_2A "Analog Port2A";
CM_ SG_ 2566854361 Port_2B "Analog Port2B";
CM_ BO_ 2566854617 "Analog ports 3A, 3B, 4A, and 4B. Documented range is 0..5000 counts for 0..5 V. This DBC scales to volts using 0.001 V per bit. When ratiometric mode is enabled, the values represent ratio voltage per the specification.";
CM_ SG_ 2566854617 Port_3A "Analog Port3A";
CM_ SG_ 2566854617 Port_3B "Analog Port3B";
CM_ SG_ 2566854617 Port_4A "Analog Port4A";
CM_ SG_ 2566854617 Port_4B "Analog Port4B";
CM_ BO_ 2566854873 "Sensor power feedback 1..4. Section 8.10 heading says PGN 65305, but the same table shows PDU Specific 0x18, which corresponds to PGN 0xFF18. This DBC uses 0x18FF18D9 to stay consistent with the PF and PS fields and the AD2/AD3 sequence.";
CM_ SG_ 2566854873 Spwr1 "Sensor Power 1 Feedback";
CM_ SG_ 2566854873 Spwr2 "Sensor Power 2 Feedback";
CM_ SG_ 2566854873 Spwr3 "Sensor Power 3 Feedback";
CM_ SG_ 2566854873 Spwr4 "Sensor Power 4 Feedback";
CM_ BO_ 2566913241 "Status message. VBAT and TEMP are encoded as 12-bit little-endian values using the low nibble of the following byte as the upper 4 bits. CNFG3 is on Byte7 and Spare is on Byte8.";
CM_ SG_ 2566913241 CNFG1 "Hardware Configuration (CNFG1)";
CM_ SG_ 2566913241 CNFG2 "PC Board Revision (CNFG2)";
CM_ SG_ 2566913241 VBAT "Battery voltage. Raw value uses 100 mV per bit with documented range 0..320, decoded here as 0.0..32.0 V.";
CM_ SG_ 2566913241 TEMP "Module temperature. Raw value uses 0.1 degF per bit with a -100 degF offset.";
CM_ SG_ 2566913241 CNFG3 "Additional Configuration (CNFG3)";
CM_ SG_ 2566913241 Spare "Spare";
CM_ BO_ 2566907609 "Fault counter message. The excerpt defines counters F1..F7 but does not map each counter slot to a specific fault code, so the counters are left as raw bytes.";
CM_ SG_ 2566907609 FLTCNT1 "Fault Counter 1";
CM_ SG_ 2566907609 FLTCNT2 "Fault Counter 2";
CM_ SG_ 2566907609 FLTCNT3 "Fault Counter 3";
CM_ SG_ 2566907609 FLTCNT4 "Fault Counter 4";
CM_ SG_ 2566907609 FLTCNT5 "Fault Counter 5";
CM_ SG_ 2566907609 FLTCNT6 "Fault Counter 6";
CM_ SG_ 2566907609 FLTCNT7 "Fault Counter 7";
CM_ BO_ 2633936089 "Wheel brake lining remaining. The DBC scales raw counts 0..250 to 0..100 percent using 0.4 percent per count. Raw value 255 is invalid or faulted. Values 251..254 are not defined by the excerpt.";
CM_ SG_ 2633936089 Count1 "D0 - Count 1";
